  "notes": "Eleven years and two production regimes, so this is two modes. `resurrection` is No I.D.'s dry MPC jazz — quantised at 0.8, one perc lane, sparse melody. `soulquarian` is the live hybrid — quantised at 0.6 with 10–12ms of jitter, snare ghosts at 0.45, and `phraseBars` reweighted to favour 8 bars, which is how the research's \"8-bar composed progressions later\" is modelled. ⛔ That is deliberate: the research names the later progressions as *longer* but gives no roman numerals for them, so this file lengthens the phrase rather than inventing chords. Base harmony is modal jazz throughout — Dorian vamps with 9th/11th colour, so `ninth` is 0.34 and the bare-`i` vamp family is researched rather than inferred. Keys sit low-mid, so `melody.register` starts at 60. The bass walks: `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.4 with five passing tones. ⚠ \"Live electric bass sitting slightly behind the beat\" has no dedicated parameter; in the `soulquarian` mode it is carried by `humanize.timingJitterMs` and a lowered `anticipationProb`. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it high-medium: the first-person interview with the defining producer covers method, not tempo or velocity. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 50 to 47 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 48 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 3.",
